Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/vn/newsroom/2026/08/apple-launches-new-education-hub-for-supplier-employees-in-vietnam/">announced</a> a new Apple Education Center in Hanoi to expand training and skill development programs for employees across its supply chain in Vietnam.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/apple-manufacturing-education-hub-vietnam-hanoi-factory.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1061388" /><br/>
The new center is the first of its kind in the country and will begin offering courses this fall, operating in partnership with Hanoi University of Science and Technology (HUST). Apple and its partners already run almost 20 educational programs for supplier employees in Vietnam. <br/>
<br/>
Courses will combine both online and in-person learning, covering areas including manufacturing, robotics, and automation technology. The center will also offer leadership and soft skills training aimed at helping workers advance in their current roles or move into new career paths.<br/>
<br/>
The new center is the latest initiative funded by Apple's &#36;50 million Supplier Employee Development Fund, a global program the company launched in 2022. Apple said more than 9 million education and training sessions have been delivered via the fund so far, and more than 108,000 supplier employees have taken part in its Swift programming courses since 2017.<br/>
<br/>
